cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NCP — Neuro-Cybernetic Protocol"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mahmoudian
    given-names: Sepehr
    email: sepehr.mahmoudian@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sepahead/NCP'
url: 'https://github.com/sepahead/NCP'
abstract: >-
  NCP couples programs that different people write, such as a spiking neural
  simulation, a simulated body or robot, and recorders, so that they work
  together in steps. NCP 2, a release candidate, makes each step run at most
  once, gives the client a true verdict after every failure, checks each
  message with a digest, and keeps a session record that a verifier can check.
  It has Python and Rust SDKs, an optional Zenoh binding, and claims proved in
  Lean. NCP 1 holds the released local SDK and the earlier wire contracts.
  Outputs are control artifacts, never validated reproductions.
keywords:
  - spiking-neural-network
  - neurorobotics
  - robotics
  - protocol
  - wire-protocol
  - nest-simulator
  - zenoh
  - closed-loop-control
  - formal-verification
  - provenance
  - pyo3
  - typescript
